# KNOWN_BEHIND: the rows of the gate where lengua isn't ahead yet (todo.md's finish line, point 4;
# src/gate.rs reads this file). A row is a runner, a workload, the version lengua is set against,
# and a measure, each a name or * for every one, and what follows a # says why:
#
# - runners: linux-x86_64, linux-aarch64, macos-aarch64, windows-x86_64, windows-aarch64;
# - workloads: empty, add, hypotenuse, upcase, upcase-stdin, shout, wc, histogram, crc32c, sort,
#   tally, server, files, readings;
# - versions: c-wasm, cpp-wasm and rust-wasm, compiled to WebAssembly and run the same way as
#   lengua's program; c, cpp and rust, built natively with the runner's own compilers;
# - measures: cpu, wall, memory, size.
#
# The list may only shrink. `cargo bench --bench against_rust_and_c` fails on a runner when it finds
# lengua behind or undecided on a row the list doesn't name, or ahead on a row it names, and it
# writes target/bench/KNOWN_BEHIND-<runner>.txt, the rows that would pass, into the run's
# artifacts. A row the gate can't decide is undecided, never level, and stays here. The bench also
# fails when a change to this file, anywhere in the history it measures, named a row the list
# before the change didn't: lines may be taken out or made narrower, never added or widened,
# except for a runner, a workload, a version or a measure the gate didn't have before.
#
# Each runner's lines below are the rows where lengua wasn't ahead in its first gate run
# (https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42661776298, at 9a549b3), which took
# the place of a line naming every row of the runner, less those where it was ahead in a later
# run: https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42728160641 (at d6496e3, lengua's
# run made lean, W12b) and https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42756074550
# (at 076bcc1, faster programs, W12c). Each line says what the latest run found.

